WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.410
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:39.880
When we arrived at Kaiba Land, someone trapped us inside a dome.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.510
We can't leave unless we defeat the Duel Computer.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.730
But the computer's level is set at max.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:54.060
My other self has to duel with a deck full of dragons, not with his own deck!

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:02.110
The Scheme Begins

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.000
Yugi…

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.930
Don't worry.  Leave it to me.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.240
Even Yugi can't win with that deck.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.850
Yeah.  The computer's level is set at max difficulty.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.480
Yugi…

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.960
Mama!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.320
Don't worry.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.110
He'll win for us.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.200
That’s right.  He's Yugi Muto, the Duel King.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.840
He won’t lose to a computer.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.920
Really?

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.740
Yeah!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.310
I know he'll do it.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:45.480
No matter how bad the situation, he always finds a way to win.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.790
You're right.  Let's believe in Yugi.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.110
My turn!

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.050
I draw!

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.920
As I expected, all monster cards.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.200
I summon Petit Dragon in defense position.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.290
I end my turn.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.070
It only has 700 defense points.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.550
And he has no set cards.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.760
He has no other cards to play.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.420
What's this?

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.880
Mokuba!

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:46.920
It’s Yugi Muto, the first Duel King who defeated Seto Kaiba at Battle City.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.140
I never thought I’d bump into him here.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.280
What a coincidence.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.840
It's a nice pre-show before the real event begins.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.160
Master Sieg.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.700
We're ready to take off.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.540
I see.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:19.250
Safe travels, Master Sieg.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.390
My turn.  I draw.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.320
I activate a spell card from my hand.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.400
Cost Down.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:47.100
By discarding a card from my hand, I lower a monster's Level by 2.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.570
Therefore, I can summon Airknight Parshath.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.970
I summon Airknight Parshath in attack position.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.910
I activate the Continuous Trap, Robbin’ Goblin.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:11.310
When my monster deals you battle damage, you must discard a card.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:15.500
Airknight Parshath attacks Petit Dragon.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.050
Airknight Parshath’s effect.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:32.360
When it attacks a monster in defense position, it deals piercing damage.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:36.420
I’m also allowed to draw a card.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:44.200
The trap card, Robbin’ Goblin’s effect activates.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.530
Please discard your rightmost card.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.440
Continuing the battle.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.070
Berserk Gorilla attacks you directly.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.970
Yugi!

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.390
This is impossible!

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.850
Wrong!  Yugi hasn’t given up!

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:13.080
Robbin’ Goblin’s continuous effect activates.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.020
Please discard the second card from the right.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.530
I end my turn.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:26.090
It’s my fault for making a deck full of dragons!

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.900
Trust the power of your deck!

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.940
But…

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.370
I believe in the faith you have in your dragons.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.310
The faith in my dragons?

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:47.410
Along with the trust in your deck, if I can draw the card my partner gave you...

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.920
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.300
A spell card.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.250
I summon Luster Dragon in attack position!

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.800
I activate the Equip Spell, Dragon Treasure from my hand!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:11.250
The equipped Dragon gains 300 attack and defense points!

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.080
Go, Luster Dragon!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.970
Attack Airknight Parshath!

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.000
Nice!  You did it, Yugi!

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.330
So there are spell cards in that deck!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.760
Wow!  He did it!  Awesome!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.700
I end my turn!

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.640
My turn.  I draw.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:42.640
When Sinister Serpent is in my graveyard during the Standby Phase, I can return it to my hand.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.240
I summon Slate Warrior in attack position.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.700
What?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:56.020
It has 1900 attack points, but it'll attack Luster Dragon's 2200 points?

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.620
The computer must be malfunctioning!

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.800
You're wrong!  It's going to...

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.330
Slate Warrior’s effect activates.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:16.190
The monster that destroyed it in battle loses 500 attack and defense points.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:23.210
It sacrificed its life points to drop my attack points.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:27.570
Berserk Gorilla attacks Luster Dragon.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:41.130
The Continuous Trap, Robbin’ Goblin's effect activates.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.670
Please discard your leftmost card.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.460
This is bad!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:54.440
Impressive.  That computer is using data from top-level duelists.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:58.010
Who’s side are you on, Otogi!

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.840
We can't get out?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.250
It’s okay.  Don’t worry.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.760
You two, knock it off.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.420
You're scaring everyone.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.360
Sorry.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.230
I end my turn.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.840
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:22.170
I summon The Dragon Dwelling in the Cave in defense position!

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:27.640
Nice!  With 2000 defense points, they can survive!

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.260
I end my turn!

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:31.810
My turn.  I draw.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.250
I tribute Berserk Gorilla.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:44.490
I summon Jinzo in attack position.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:51.280
It can summon Jinzo?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:57.980
Like I said, that computer holds data on every card and duelist in the world!

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:03.000
Jinzo attacks The Dragon Dwelling in the Cave.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.060
I end my turn.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:13.110
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.600
That card is...

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:21.040
Your deck has responded to your trust!

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.960
What card did he draw?

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.290
Yugi…

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:30.380
I summon Baby Dragon in defense position!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:39.590
I activate the Continuous Spell, Heart of the Underdog from my hand!

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:42.670
This is my key card!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.940
U-Underdog?

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.980
That doesn't look useful.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.260
I see!  That's his plan!

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:13.550
Not bad!

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.220
I end my turn!

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:18.150
My turn.  I draw.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.650
I summon Sinister Serpent in attack position.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:28.260
Jinzo attacks Baby Dragon.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:34.300
Sinister Serpent attacks you directly.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.870
I end my turn.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.810
Here we go.  It’s my turn!

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:44.750
I draw!

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:50.590
The Continuous Spell, Heart of the Underdog’s effect activates!

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:59.060
If I drew a Normal Monster, I can show it to you to draw another card.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:03.270
I drew this!  Curse of Dragon!

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.200
I draw another card.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.140
Koumori Dragon!

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:08.440
I draw!

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.510
Winged Dragon, Guardian of the Fortress #1!

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.220
I draw!  Hyozanryu!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.950
I draw!  Crawling Dragon!

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.530
I draw!  Blackland Fire Dragon!

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.460
I draw!

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:25.440
I summon Spirit Ryu in attack position!

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.600
Spirit Ryu attacks Jinzo!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.240
Spirit Ryu’s effect now activates!

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:47.740
Every time I discard a Dragon-Type monster during battle, it gains 1000 attack and defense points!

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:52.200
I have six Dragon-Type monsters in my hand.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.480
It gains 6000 attack points!

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.350
Continue the battle!

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.700
Go, Spirit Ryu!

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.530
Spirit Burst!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.720
You did it, Yugi!

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:19.940
He won with that deck?  Wow!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.380
Yugi is incredible!

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.540
We're saved.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:24.320
You did it!

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:33.130
Rick, keep believing in your monsters.

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:35.430
Right!  Thank you!

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.460
Wow!  Your deck is actually strong!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:43.200
Maybe I'll collect Dragon-Types too!

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:55.000
No wonder he was able to defeat Seto Kaiba.

00:13:58.050 --> 00:14:01.050
It’s great to be outside!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.140
Yeah.  I was worried for a bit.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.050
Thank you, Yugi!

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:07.680
I’ll treasure this card!

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.560
Right.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.180
Bye!

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.240
Dad!  Mom!  It was awesome!

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.130
Yugi, what’s up with that card?

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.330
Why did you have it?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:22.060
Umm...  Well uh...

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.420
You handle this.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.260
Huh?

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.610
That’s not fair, my other self!

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.150
Yugi!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:32.610
You think I’m an underdog too?

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:34.270
O-Of course not.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.920
I thought that spell's effect was useful.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:41.400
Though it does sorta remind me of you-

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.200
C'mon, it's fine.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.650
Because the underdog came in handy.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.600
You're one to talk!

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.070
Mokuba!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.020
Big brother!

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:57.500
Are you okay, Mokuba?

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.510
Kaiba!

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:02.510
Kaiba!  You just arrived?

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:06.950
Your Duel Computer put us in danger!

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:08.890
Stop barking, underdog.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.130
It wasn’t my fault.

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:17.290
Someone hacked into my company's systems.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.540
Big brother…

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:20.060
Don’t worry, Mokuba.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.760
I got rid of the intruder.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.500
Whoever did this isn't happy...

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:31.310
...that Kaiba Corporation has regained the public's trust with the success of the KC Grand Prix.

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:34.750
But I’ll make them regret challenging me!

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:40.590
Recheck all of Kaiba Land to make sure it's safe.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:43.470
I don't want any more interruptions.

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:46.430
The KC Grand Prix must be a success.

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.190
Yes, right away.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.440
You all can do whatever you want.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.540
Mokuba, you're in charge.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.910
You're so arrogant!

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:03.170
The tournament would fail without us!

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.980
So many people!

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:18.940
Kaiba Corporation is hosting this duel tournament.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:22.840
The world is focused on this event, so there's a lot of media here.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:23.930
What?

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:27.110
Hey!  Shizuka, see me?

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:28.900
Stop it, Honda!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.050
Shizuka, it's your brother!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:35.470
You two are so immature.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.280
Looks delicious!

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:40.590
Be more careful!

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:43.350
You should watch where you're going!

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.780
What's wrong, Rebecca?

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.300
This girl-

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.890
Are you Yugi Muto?

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:51.960
Y-Yes.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.350
I knew it!  I’m so happy!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:56.330
I wanted to meet you.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.500
I’m Vivian Wong.  Nice to meet you.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:03.360
What’s with her!

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.850
I’m happy to meet a famous duelist like you!

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:10.080
We’re rivals during the tournament.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.810
But we can be friendly in private!

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:17.900
Hey you!

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.410
Don’t cuddle with my darling!

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:25.190
Hey, it’s President Kaiba!  He's fabulous!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.620
What's with her?

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:28.910
Yugi!

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:30.970
Hi, Leon!

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:32.600
Why are you here?

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:35.610
I’m also in the KC Grand Prix.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:36.900
You too?

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.530
Yes.  I'm so happy!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:43.340
I may get a chance to duel you, Yugi!

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:46.010
If we do, let's give it our all!

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.950
All the duelists aren't here yet?

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.380
We're waiting for one more.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:58.510
Then he's disqualified.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.750
Let's begin, Isono.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:02.220
But…

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:02.980
Excuse me.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.160
I’m Zieg Lloyd.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.700
Sorry I'm late.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:11.150
Thank you for the invitation, Mr. Kaiba.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:18.570
All the duelists participating in the tournament have arrived, Isono.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.450
Yes sir!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.640
Thank you for your patience.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:30.760
We'll now begin the KC Grand Prix's opening ceremonies - hosted by Kaiba Corporation!

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.680
To determine the strongest duelist!

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:37.630
Duelists, please gather to the stage.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.680
Let’s go, Yugi.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.460
Right.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:52.050
After a careful selection process, these are the most powerful duelists in the world.

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:55.040
First, the overnight sensation!

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.750
Undefeated in every tournament he's entered!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:02.400
The young prodigy, Leon Wilson!

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:06.090
He's a famous duelist?

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:12.020
The mysterious prophet who controls the fate of the cards, Fortune Salim!

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:15.340
His tactics are like the drifting clouds!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:18.480
The wandering duelist, Essel Jansen!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:22.340
The assassin from the north, Sergei Ivanoff!

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:28.080
A keen mind with excellent deductive and observational skills!

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:31.550
The detective duelist, Paul McGregor!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:35.730
The wild risktaker, Abe!

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.780
Will his instincts help him win?

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:45.060
He wins his duels with surgical precision!  Dr. Richard Goat!

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:48.820
Unrivaled in using magic cards!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:51.940
The magic master, Barry Ginger!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.170
Actually, this is the master of magic!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:01.600
When he wields his cards, he blurs the line between dueling and illusion!

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.180
Theodore Iwalos!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.460
His duels are street fights!

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:09.930
The man-eating shark from the south seas, Ethan Shark!

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:13.360
The enlightened duelist, Jafar Shin!

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.530
Asia's gorgeous flower!

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.460
It’s her!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.330
Vivian Wong!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:26.070
America's youngest-ever champ, Rebecca Hopkins!

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:33.120
Top 4 in Battle City, the duelist of fire!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.950
The underdog, Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.620
Who are you calling underdog!

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:42.020
His achievements and identity are a mystery!

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:45.060
The legendary duelist, Mask the Rock!

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:46.580
Isn't that...

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.490
C-Can it be?

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:53.440
Europe's undefeated nobleman, the Emperor Zieg Lloyd!

00:20:56.680 --> 00:21:01.300
And our returning champion from Battle City, Yugi Muto!

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:09.180
As our defending champion, he'll face the tournament winner to see who's the true Duel King!

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.730
In order to duel Yugi, you have to win the tournament?

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.190
That'll be tough.

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:22.700
The computer will randomly choose the matchups before each duel.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:26.560
So you don’t know who you’ll face until right before the duel.

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:30.800
It doesn’t matter who I face!  I'm gonna win!

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:09.650
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:18.020
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:29.180
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:38.670
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:39.270 --> 00:22:47.730
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:53.240
I'll live feeling them

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:58.390
For me to be me

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:06.880
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:12.520
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:22.180
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:30.730
The KC Grand Prix finally begins!

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:35.180
Jonouchi is in the first match of the tournament.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:38.550
His opponent is... Mask the Rock?

00:23:38.550 --> 00:23:41.740
It's obvious who he is...

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:44.770
Why did he enter this tournament?

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:47.450
Jonouchi, stop wasting time!

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:51.190
If you don't get to the location in time, you'll be disqualified!

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:54.800
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Jonouchi vs Mask the Rock

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.310
Duel, standby!
